 "built": "2026-10-14",
 "method": "Revised 2026 registered voter benchmarks, statewide, Oct 14 2026.\n\nThree sources, each strong where the others are weak:\n  1. Bonfire voter file counts, all 50 states: registrants by age band, education, race and sex. A hard count of\n     the registered universe, with age and sex from the record itself, race self reported in the six states that\n     ask it on the form (AL, FL, GA, LA, NC, SC) and modeled elsewhere, and education modeled and coarse (its\n     \"High School\" holds everyone without a degree, so it cannot split high school from some college). The file\n     carries inactive and moved registrants, so in several states it exceeds the citizen adult population.\n  2. The model's own registered voter estimate, the one the forecast reports for each state: census citizen\n     adults (Census CVAP special tabulation, 2020 to 2024 ACS, by county and race group) times the TPSI\n     registration rate fitted on respondents by age, race, college and region.\n  3. The census itself for education detail: ACS 2020 to 2024 S1501 educational attainment by state, weighted by\n     the TPSI registration rate for each education level.\n\nTotals. Registered = citizen adults times a registration rate, the rate a blend in log odds of the file's rate\n(capped at 97 percent of citizen adults, since a file above that is carrying deadwood) at FILE_W_TOTAL and the\nmodel's rate at the rest.\n\nComposition. Every margin is the file's share and the estimate's share blended, the file weighted by how much its\nfield can be trusted: age 0.75 (0.55 where more than 15 percent of ages are suppressed, 0.35 where a band is off the\ncensus by more than 6 points), sex 1.0, race 0.85 where\nrace is self reported and 0.35 where it is modeled, since surname models overcount Hispanic registrants\n(0.10 less where more than 20 percent is unknown), degree\nholding 0.35 and graduate share among degree holders 0.35. The high school or less against some college split is\ncensus only. Unknown and blank values are left out of the file's shares rather than guessed. The age by gender\ncells are the file's joint table raked to the blended age and sex margins.\nOutputs aggregate tables only; no respondent row leaves this script.",
